Counting Photons
================

Group: Astrostatistics

Open index.html directly (file://), or serve it beside TeachingTools. Native
offline HTML/Canvas/JavaScript; no Shiny, WebR, CDN, modules or installation.
app.R and model.R remain unchanged reference sources.

Principle: exact Poisson fluctuations are discrete and asymmetric at low counts;
a Gaussian is an approximation, never the sampler. For known constant rate r
and elapsed exposure t, N~Poisson(lambda=r*t), E[N]=Var[N]=lambda, SD=sqrt(lambda),
relative SD=1/sqrt(lambda) for positive lambda. This is a sampling model, not an
interval inferred from the realised stream. No background, detector dead time,
saturation, clustering or time variation is modelled.

Two random experiments, cached playback
---------------------------------------
The stream uses exact exponential waiting times -log(U)/r. A seed fixes
unit-rate event times through the largest supported optical exposure (160);
rate rescales those times, and exposure reveals their prefix. A separate set
of 3000 seeded uniforms is inverse-transformed using the Poisson recurrence
at each of 61 cached frames. Fixed quantiles couple successive histogram
frames monotonically; these are NOT 3000 event timelines with independent
increments. Only the displayed stream is an actual Poisson event timeline.

All frames are cached. Playback/scrubbing and the Show/Hide Gaussian choice
never resample data. New realisation advances the seeded Astro RNG; Reset
restores defaults. The original R/browser RNG sequences intentionally differ.

Gaussian comparison and native differences
-------------------------------------------
Preserves the original 60 steps, 3000 replicates, rate/exposure controls,
few/many presets, continuity correction and lecture link. Adds a zero-rate
dark-source example and empirical mean/variance alongside the theoretical
expectation/variance. Zero rate/exposure yields a point mass at zero, SD zero,
undefined relative SD and no nondegenerate Gaussian.

Normal comparison masses integrate each integer bin [k-.5,k+.5], so they are
comparable to Poisson masses and empirical frequencies, not density heights.
The negative tail is not removed or renormalised; P(Normal<-.5) is displayed
even when the curve is hidden. All observed counts are shown; theoretical
outer tails may be outside the finite plot window without renormalisation.
The inverse-CDF implementation supports the full control range 0<=lambda<=160
using floating-point recurrence, not a large-lambda Normal approximation.
Independent uniform/event streams remove an incidental retained-R coupling in
which changing rate changed how many RNG values preceded the count quantiles.

Numerical API (model.js, browser PhotonCountingModel and CommonJS)
---------------------------------------------------------------
defaults; STEPS=60; REPEATS=3000; MAX_LAMBDA=160; validate(parameters)
poissonPmf(integerCount, lambda), poissonTable(lambda) -> {pmf,cdf}
poissonQuantile(probability, lambda) -> integer (Infinity for p=1, lambda>0)
gaussianMass(integerCount, lambda) -> continuity-corrected mass (null at zero)
prepare(seed) -> seed, fixed uniforms and unit-rate arrival times
compute(parameters, optionalPrepared) -> cached frames, stream and metadata
atFrame(result, integerFrame) -> elapsed exposure, lambda, arrivals, counts,
  empirical moments, exact/Normal masses, negative mass and plot support
Invalid values throw Astro.ValidationError. Parameters: seed integer
0..2147483647, rate 0..8, exposure 0.5..20, gaussian show/hide.

Validation (from the repository root)
------------------------------------
node PhotonCounting/test_model.js
node PhotonCounting/test_browser.js
Numerics use independently R-calibrated qpois/dpois/pnorm/qexp values (including
extreme quantiles at lambda=160), sampling moments, low-count approximation
failure, monotone coupled histograms, stream prefixes, zero rate/exposure,
seed stability and boundaries. Chrome verifies plotted distributions, actual
arrival marks, cached Show/Hide/playback, metrics, errors, mobile and file://.
For a repository-local Chrome profile, create PhotonCounting/.browser-state,
set TMPDIR to its absolute path for the test, then remove the empty directory.

Runtime assets: index.html, model.js, app.js, plus
../TeachingTools/{statistics.js,browser.js,browser.css,lesson.js}. No others.
